  "prefLabel": "Ins 6203.02 Definitions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 6203.02 Definitions.\n\n(a) “Accident-only coverage” means a policy or certificate that provides coverage, singularly or in combination, for death, dismemberment, disability, or hospital and medical care caused by accident.\n\n(b) “Specified accident coverage” means a group policy or certificate that provides coverage for death, dismemberment, disability, or hospital and medical care caused by a specifically identified kind of accident or accidents for each person covered under the policy, either singularly or in combination.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Ins 6200) #12855, eff 8-26-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins6200.html"
